WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.480
I'm Angela Lee-Smith.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.070
I teach Korean and English
at the East Asian Languages

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.620
and Literatures department.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:14.240
Today, the summary of
my presentation is--

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.880
oops.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.820
I try go to the next slide.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:23.320
Sorry.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.772
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:27.192
You should be able to.

00:00:27.192 --> 00:00:28.160
Oh.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.520
[INAUDIBLE] OK.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.060
So I implemented audio
portfolios my students.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:42.470
And these portfolios are
perfect examples of progress

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.330
in evidenced-based approach.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.310
And I use Canvas tool
audio-video submission.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.200
And it is totally
free, just for you.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.084
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.800
So why portfolios?

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.770
Because we oftentimes
face great challenges

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:05.440
to ensure every students
progress and achieve something

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.910
after the semester.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.790
So we need some kind
of instructional tools

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:18.020
to identify how to adjust
[INAUDIBLE] strategies.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:20.780
And as you all know,
we have a slogan

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.930
that, No Child Left Behind.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:27.870
And that applies even in this
higher education environment.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:32.450
So as I said, portfolios
allows me to practice progress

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.970
in evidence-based
teaching practice

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:41.840
and makes learning as a
continued and ongoing process.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.950
So as you see here,
this is the example

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:49.550
of elementary
Korean course site.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.030
And I assigned four
portfolio assignment.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:57.790
So every two weeks, students
record their speaking

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.829
on the given topics in
a day, just to submit.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.730
And this is the
instructor's site.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:11.360
And you see students
have two choices.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.600
They can either submit
audio files, or video files.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.550
Some students
prefer video files,

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.580
so they get to see their
messy dorm room background.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.920
[LAUGHTER]

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.900
And then, once they submit
their speaking file,

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.830
I get to listen to their
file and analyze and then

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:33.300
immediately provide my feedback.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.330
And so this one,
I can either type,

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.470
or I can even
upload my speaking.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.330
So especially, for an
elementary language course,

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:47.050
the pronunciation
is very critical.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.440
So that really helps.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:55.700
So Canvas built-in
audio-video submission tool

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.570
really allows me to use
my students' performance

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:02.650
data to check their progress.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.600
And then, help me
make more informed

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.240
instructional decisions.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.240
And I can monitor my
students very closely

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.180
and provide them with
frequent feedback.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:17.360
So is this totally
stress-free and worth it.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.230
And let's utilize it more.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.170
That's it.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.880
Any questions?

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.205
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:24.205 --> 00:03:27.440
So like sales piece for Canvas.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.880
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.570
And then you get 24-7,
non-stop support.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.070
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:36.560
Yes.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.060
Yes?

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.268
Did you have students
[INAUDIBLE] about the interface

00:03:39.268 --> 00:03:40.000
at all?

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.380
Or did you have to
help students with it?

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:42.920
Not ever.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.850
This is very easy.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:51.880
They get to see the button,
either audio recording,

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:56.230
or video clip recorded,
and then Submit button.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.078
That's it.

00:03:57.078 --> 00:03:57.578
Yeah.

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:01.934
Yes?

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.838
And you mentioned
that it's stress-free?

00:04:04.838 --> 00:04:05.820
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.240
Yes.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.740
I don't know how many students
you have in your class, but--

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:10.801
30.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:11.300
30.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.341
There are three sections.

00:04:12.341 --> 00:04:17.480
So it must be a stress for you
to give each one a feedback?

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.320
Do you record audio
files to feed back?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.400
Only for the necessary cases.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:23.900
Oh.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:24.470
Yes.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.360
But I listen every single one.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:26.930
Right.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.250
Every two weeks.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.860
And it's not stress at all.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:31.782
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:31.782 --> 00:04:33.165
Yes?

00:04:33.165 --> 00:04:35.940
So you give feedback
to everybody?

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:36.826
Yes.

00:04:36.826 --> 00:04:38.450
You do give feedback?

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:42.710
I give every single
one feedback, yes.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.400
Even though it's not
good, I say, good, but--

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.370
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:50.350
Yeah.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.730
So it's a very rewarding
experience, both for me

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.500
and students.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.550
So at the end of
semester, students

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.270
get to listen to
their from day one

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.540
file to the end of the file.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.810
And then, they can
clearly listen and see

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.836
how they improved.

00:05:07.836 --> 00:05:10.910
So it's a really
rewarding experience.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.696
Yes?

00:05:11.696 --> 00:05:13.154
Actually, [INAUDIBLE]
answer that.

00:05:13.154 --> 00:05:16.556
So you said these are
restricted to you?

00:05:16.556 --> 00:05:19.715
Is there a way to have
them so the students could

00:05:19.715 --> 00:05:22.880
see each other, to do some
sort of peer evaluations?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:28.230
That's only for the 101
tutorial session with the TAs.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:30.650
So the TA get to
listen to each file.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:31.680
And then, they share.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.020
And then, only
every two weeks, we

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.860
get to have the session
[INAUDIBLE] time.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:45.200
So we get to pick some
files I would really like

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.050
to get students' attention.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.112
And then, we practice together.

00:05:49.112 --> 00:05:49.611
OK.

00:05:49.611 --> 00:05:53.510
So you have to pick which ones
the other students can see.

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:54.010
Yes.

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:54.986
OK.

00:05:54.986 --> 00:05:55.486
Yeah.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:00.560
Yes?

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:06.208
I think it is possible in
Canvas to have a peer evaluation

00:06:06.208 --> 00:06:09.770
type of design there,
but you might not

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.430
want to do that at the 101.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:15.330
Yeah, I do use the function,
because the students usually--

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:19.500
even very hard to listen to
their own voice, so they say,

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:20.100
no.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:25.180
So we just get together, and
then go through it together.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.200
Yeah.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.590
[INAUDIBLE]

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:31.860
Some of my students had
a technical problem when

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.300
they are recording themselves.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:37.292
And I asked them to
ask [INAUDIBLE] people.

00:06:37.292 --> 00:06:41.450
And then, I don't know if you
have any problem like that.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.880
Before using Canvas, I
had the same problem,

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.070
because the students
used their phone

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:48.290
and tried to upload their file.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:51.235
But they used laptop, and
they use the Canvas tool.

00:06:51.235 --> 00:06:52.110
Yeah, but [INAUDIBLE]

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.627
And they don't have to upload--

00:06:53.627 --> 00:06:54.127
Right.

00:06:54.127 --> 00:06:54.627
Right.

00:06:54.627 --> 00:06:56.935
They couldn't record
on the screen.

00:06:56.935 --> 00:06:58.268
I don't know what's the problem.

00:06:58.268 --> 00:07:00.836
And the Canvas people
said they're trying

00:07:00.836 --> 00:07:04.067
to figure out the problem.

00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:08.043
I'm wondering if
that's been fixed.

00:07:08.043 --> 00:07:11.530
As far as I know,
we did testing,

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.740
and we couldn't find
any issues ourselves.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.510
So it might be configurations
on their own laptops or machines

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:18.730
that they're using.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.582
But we'd be happy to have
them bring in their laptops

00:07:21.582 --> 00:07:22.540
and have us look at it.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.270
But the system seems to be
working for other students,

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.670
so it must be specific to
whatever configuration's

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.460
on their machines.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:32.934
So if they have a problem,
just go to Kimberly.

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:33.434
[LAUGHTER]

00:07:33.434 --> 00:07:34.398
Yes.

00:07:34.398 --> 00:07:34.898
Jen.

00:07:34.898 --> 00:07:35.874
Where is Jen?

00:07:35.874 --> 00:07:38.610
[LAUGHTER]

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:39.110
OK.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:39.650
Thank you.

